1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:19,031
Mutta Jongsawat, she has a history of unprotected sex.

9
00:00:19,083 --> 00:00:22,680
She's been diagnosed with gonorrhea.

10
00:00:24,142 --> 00:00:25,400
Mutta has this disease?

11
00:00:25,443 --> 00:00:27,880
Don't ever abuse your authority to hurt Mutta again.

12
00:00:27,955 --> 00:00:30,360
- Should I be scared?
- I'll announce to the media

13
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:31,960
that you and I

14
00:00:32,131 --> 00:00:34,760
are no longer husband and wife.

15
00:00:34,856 --> 00:00:36,000
Are you starting to get scared?

16
00:00:36,504 --> 00:00:37,520
The test results are in.

17
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,421
Syphilis, gonorrhea, HPV, and HIV. All negative.

18
00:00:41,795 --> 00:00:44,320
Whoever's trying to frame me like this, stop it.

19
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:45,681
It's pathetic.

20
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:46,721
- We know!
- We know!

21
00:00:46,741 --> 00:00:48,960
Does she seriously not care that she's been exposed for having gonorrhea?

22
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:51,208
That's right. Her results came back negative,

23
00:00:51,249 --> 00:00:53,600
and nobody's gossiping about it anymore.

24
00:00:53,886 --> 00:00:56,680
She seems awfully proud of the ring Phop gave her,

25
00:00:56,771 --> 00:00:59,072
when there should only be one ring.

26
00:00:59,082 --> 00:01:01,790
Then let's use that ring to hurt her.

27
00:01:01,843 --> 00:01:03,600
- Police?
- Hello.

28
00:01:03,955 --> 00:01:05,606
You're Mutta Jongsawat, correct?

29
00:01:05,672 --> 00:01:07,720
May I see both your hands, please?

30
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:09,760
You've been accused of stealing this ring.

31
00:01:09,923 --> 00:01:11,200
Please come with us to the police station.

32
00:01:11,358 --> 00:01:12,960
Hong, aren't they two different rings?

33
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,840
Then would you dare testify for Ta, Whiskey?

34
00:01:49,872 --> 00:01:50,873
Huh?

35
00:01:52,358 --> 00:01:53,359
Where are you going, Ta?

36
00:01:55,899 --> 00:01:56,900
Oh.

37
00:01:58,027 --> 00:01:59,947
You want to do it on the balcony, huh?

38
00:02:00,491 --> 00:02:01,492
Sure, let's go.

39
00:02:04,092 --> 00:02:05,360
That's not it, Director.

40
00:02:09,211 --> 00:02:10,880
I think we should end things here.

41
00:02:12,975 --> 00:02:14,560
I can't take this anymore.

42
00:02:15,056 --> 00:02:16,057
Huh?

43
00:02:18,262 --> 00:02:19,320
Did I hurt you, Ta?

44
00:02:21,728 --> 00:02:22,760
I'm sorry.

45
00:02:23,624 --> 00:02:24,625
Then...

46
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,160
I'll be gentler this time.

47
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,921
No, that's not it.

48
00:02:33,854 --> 00:02:36,200
I can't live with this guilt anymore.

49
00:02:41,534 --> 00:02:43,760
I don't want to be known as anyone's mistress.

50
00:02:46,392 --> 00:02:48,560
Let's stop seeing each other outside of work.

51
00:02:50,851 --> 00:02:51,852
Oh, come on.

52
00:02:53,803 --> 00:02:54,804
Ta.

53
00:02:55,206 --> 00:02:58,448
In just a few years, my kids will all be grown up.

54
00:02:59,136 --> 00:03:02,400
When that day comes, I'll pack my things and move in here with you.

55
00:03:04,336 --> 00:03:05,337
Please wait for me.

56
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:06,701
Please.

57
00:03:08,512 --> 00:03:10,213
Then why don't we wait until that day comes

58
00:03:10,912 --> 00:03:12,520
before we see each other again?

59
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:17,840
I can't wait that long, Ta.

60
00:03:18,651 --> 00:03:20,400
Can you really bear to wait?

61
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,720
Then I'll resign.

62
00:03:27,323 --> 00:03:29,184
Maybe if we stop seeing each other,

63
00:03:30,486 --> 00:03:32,360
we'll stop missing each other so much.

64
00:03:34,283 --> 00:03:36,480
Or if you don't truly love me,

65
00:03:38,688 --> 00:03:41,089
we can finally cut ties for good.

66
00:03:42,187 --> 00:03:43,188
Ta.

67
00:04:09,158 --> 00:04:11,136
I've been looking for the right moment to surprise you.

68
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:18,391
Ta.

69
00:04:35,536 --> 00:04:37,640
Please stop doubting my love for you.

70
00:04:46,371 --> 00:04:47,960
I'll wait for you, Director.

71
00:04:53,134 --> 00:04:54,135
This ring...

72
00:04:56,507 --> 00:04:58,360
Don't wear it outside where anyone can see it.

73
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,280
Especially my wife.

74
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:18,191
He told me never to wear the ring outside.

75
00:05:19,104 --> 00:05:20,840
But I wore it just once,

76
00:05:21,536 --> 00:05:22,960
and his wife saw it.

77
00:05:23,787 --> 00:05:25,000
She was furious.

78
00:05:25,824 --> 00:05:27,720
She slapped me so hard I tumbled down the stairs.

79
00:05:28,443 --> 00:05:31,104
Everyone just stood there watching like it was a circus.

80
00:05:32,534 --> 00:05:34,400
She ordered everyone to keep their mouths shut

81
00:05:35,115 --> 00:05:37,250
and had all the security footage erased.

82
00:05:38,352 --> 00:05:40,080
I'm just a tiny little ant

83
00:05:40,774 --> 00:05:42,840
being crushed by an elephant.

84
00:05:43,995 --> 00:05:47,160
She has the power to summon every beast in the jungle

85
00:05:47,432 --> 00:05:49,250
to attack me whenever she wants.

86
00:05:49,747 --> 00:05:52,560
How could I possibly fight back?

87
00:05:56,411 --> 00:05:57,412
Don't worry.

88
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,441
This little ant

89
00:06:00,358 --> 00:06:01,659
will bring that elephant down.

90
00:07:20,384 --> 00:07:21,560
No, Ta. You've got it all wrong.

91
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:24,235
I had this ring custom-made for you.

92
00:07:24,976 --> 00:07:26,288
It definitely isn't Nopnapha's.

93
00:07:27,678 --> 00:07:29,920
Ta... Calm down. I'm on my way.

94
00:07:31,366 --> 00:07:32,367
Director, sir.

95
00:07:32,969 --> 00:07:35,480
The Director-General has asked me to invite you to discuss next year's policies.

96
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,280
This is the asset declaration

97
00:07:40,494 --> 00:07:43,200
Nopnapha submitted before taking office.

98
00:07:44,259 --> 00:07:46,260
It clearly lists the details of the ring.

99
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:48,760
And this is the diamond certificate.

100
00:07:50,638 --> 00:07:51,639
What about yours?

101
00:07:57,627 --> 00:07:59,300
When someone gives you a gift,

102
00:07:59,712 --> 00:08:01,648
they don't usually include the receipt, you know.

103
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:05,360
All I got was the ring. I didn't even get the box.

104
00:08:06,008 --> 00:08:08,250
Because he slipped it right onto my finger.

105
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,601
I mean,

106
00:08:11,624 --> 00:08:12,960
Director Jenphop did.

107
00:08:13,867 --> 00:08:17,200
Are you saying that Ms.Nopnapha's husband

108
00:08:18,182 --> 00:08:19,600
stole this ring and gave it to you?

109
00:08:20,358 --> 00:08:21,359
No.

110
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:24,640
He just had an identical ring made for me.

111
00:08:25,814 --> 00:08:28,240
So where is Director Jenphop?

112
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:30,080
Is he coming or not?

113
00:08:46,998 --> 00:08:48,000
You can't do that, Uncle.

114
00:08:48,438 --> 00:08:50,640
If you don't show up, who's going to testify for Ta?

115
00:08:51,078 --> 00:08:52,650
Besides, you're the one who caused all this.

116
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,600
Sending someone else isn't the same as coming yourself.

117
00:08:59,307 --> 00:09:00,920
Hold on, Uncle. Tetris is calling.

118
00:09:04,272 --> 00:09:05,273
Hello, Tetris.

119
00:09:05,302 --> 00:09:08,280
Where are you, Veekit? Why are you taking so long today?

120
00:09:08,651 --> 00:09:10,790
Sorry, Tetris. Something came up.

121
00:09:11,632 --> 00:09:14,000
Can you get a ride home by yourself?

122
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:15,731
And take good care of your sister.

123
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:17,520
Oh, okay.

124
00:09:19,064 --> 00:09:20,165
Veekit said we can go home on our own.

125
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,120
- Yay!
- Hey!

126
00:09:22,936 --> 00:09:24,880
He said go home, not go partying!

127
00:09:25,446 --> 00:09:27,440
I'm taking the bus home. Let go!

128
00:09:27,622 --> 00:09:29,960
No way. I'm just booking a ride.

129
00:09:30,288 --> 00:09:32,864
Then go ahead. I can take the bus by myself.

130
00:09:34,734 --> 00:09:35,735
Hey!

131
00:09:36,334 --> 00:09:37,640
Wait for me, you bitch!

132
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:42,000
So, is the man who gave you the ring coming or not?

133
00:09:48,742 --> 00:09:50,091
Director Jenphop has an urgent matter to attend to.

134
00:09:53,019 --> 00:09:55,240
So he sent a gemologist in his place.

135
00:10:06,443 --> 00:10:10,640
According to the certificate, Ms. Nopnapha's diamond is graded VVS1.

136
00:10:10,854 --> 00:10:12,822
That means it has very slight internal inclusions.

137
00:10:13,088 --> 00:10:15,089
As for Mutta's ring,

138
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:16,800
the diamond is graded Flawless.

139
00:10:16,851 --> 00:10:19,091
That means it has no internal or external flaws.

140
00:10:19,539 --> 00:10:21,480
We can confirm they're different diamonds

141
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:24,401
because their laser-inscribed identification numbers don't match.

142
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:28,000
So they're two different rings with different diamond grades.

143
00:10:33,971 --> 00:10:36,520
Sir, the police have released Mutta.

144
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,341
Yes, ma'am.

145
00:10:45,016 --> 00:10:47,240
Where's the Director-General?

146
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,238
I've been waiting for an hour!

147
00:10:50,278 --> 00:10:51,760
He's asked to postpone the meeting to another day.

148
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:54,520
- What?
- He also asked me to apologize on his behalf.

149
00:10:55,201 --> 00:10:56,480
What the hell?

150
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,440
What's his problem?

151
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:10,500
Ta... How did it go?

152
00:11:12,859 --> 00:11:15,078
Everything's settled. It's all over now.

153
00:11:15,659 --> 00:11:17,060
Thanks for not showing up,

154
00:11:18,014 --> 00:11:19,475
but at least going to the trouble of sending someone in your place.

155
00:11:20,286 --> 00:11:21,720
Ta, I'm really sorry.

156
00:11:22,286 --> 00:11:24,720
I'm done with my business now. Where are you, Ta?

157
00:11:25,102 --> 00:11:26,160
I'll come see you right away.

158
00:11:26,616 --> 00:11:29,440
It's okay. I'm with Veekit. Bye.

159
00:11:30,734 --> 00:11:32,640
Ma'am, she's out now.

160
00:11:35,011 --> 00:11:35,712
Ta.

161
00:11:35,715 --> 00:11:39,160
That lying bitch has such a slap-worthy face, ma'am!

162
00:11:42,414 --> 00:11:43,880
You've heard about it, haven't you?

163
00:11:44,312 --> 00:11:46,560
That our diamonds are of different grades.

164
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:48,360
Now you know

165
00:11:48,651 --> 00:11:51,880
which woman your husband loves more.

166
00:11:55,622 --> 00:11:57,430
Ma'am, are you okay?

167
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,840
Who pissed you off, ma'am? Hello?

168
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,883
What made you decide to wear that ring today?

169
00:12:01,963 --> 00:12:03,240
I told you not to wear it, didn't I?

170
00:12:03,707 --> 00:12:05,880
I only wear it when I'm with you, Director.

171
00:12:07,110 --> 00:12:08,440
It would be such a shame

172
00:12:08,827 --> 00:12:10,880
to keep something this beautiful locked away in a box.

173
00:12:15,910 --> 00:12:17,200
Let me tell you a little secret.

174
00:12:17,714 --> 00:12:18,715
This ring,

175
00:12:19,755 --> 00:12:21,720
even though it looks just like Nopnapha's,

176
00:12:23,216 --> 00:12:25,920
has a diamond of much higher quality.

177
00:12:34,667 --> 00:12:36,107
Oshi, please go check on Aunt Nopnapha.

178
00:12:37,046 --> 00:12:38,528
And get her some medicine for her sore throat, too.

179
00:12:50,843 --> 00:12:53,174
Thanks. Sorry for wasting your time.

180
00:12:55,979 --> 00:12:57,899
It's okay. I wasn't busy anyway.

181
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,504
But could you please stop wearing that ring?

182
00:13:07,534 --> 00:13:09,235
I hardly ever see you wearing it anyway.

183
00:13:10,091 --> 00:13:11,700
Every time you do, it causes trouble.

184
00:13:12,331 --> 00:13:13,800
I'm not the one causing trouble.

185
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:16,071
You should be blaming your aunt instead.

186
00:13:17,094 --> 00:13:19,280
If I confront Aunt Nopnapha, she'll just turn around and blame you.

187
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,500
She'll say you went after her husband first, Ta.

188
00:13:23,472 --> 00:13:25,773
Seriously, do you think there's any chance

189
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,628
you'll stop seeing Uncle Phop?

190
00:13:31,254 --> 00:13:32,255
Of course there is.

191
00:13:33,174 --> 00:13:34,440
Just not anytime soon.

192
00:13:35,552 --> 00:13:38,760
Then when, Ta? What are you waiting for?

193
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:42,071
I've got to go.

194
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:43,681
Ta.

195
00:13:45,155 --> 00:13:47,859
Wanna grab some dim sum in Thonglor? My treat.

196
00:13:49,016 --> 00:13:51,240
Your treat? What's the occasion?

197
00:13:54,016 --> 00:13:55,480
To cheer you up after getting arrested.

198
00:13:59,494 --> 00:14:01,480
Nah, I don't like dim sum.

199
00:14:02,650 --> 00:14:04,890
If you don't want to go, at least come up with a better excuse.

200
00:14:07,350 --> 00:14:08,960
You've been to that restaurant with Uncle Phop plenty of times.

201
00:14:09,318 --> 00:14:12,280
I know because I made the reservations myself.

202
00:14:13,414 --> 00:14:14,920
Uncle Phop told me you loved that place.

203
00:14:15,579 --> 00:14:17,720
I used to, but I don't anymore.

204
00:14:18,059 --> 00:14:19,400
People can change, can't they?

205
00:14:21,078 --> 00:14:22,600
Is that really the reason?

206
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,536
You look different. Did you get a haircut?

207
00:14:36,286 --> 00:14:37,920
Do I look pretty? Do you like it?

208
00:14:38,467 --> 00:14:39,468
You look cute.

209
00:14:42,192 --> 00:14:44,680
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

210
00:14:44,872 --> 00:14:47,131
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

211
00:14:47,424 --> 00:14:49,920
♪ Happy birthday, my love ♪

212
00:14:50,048 --> 00:14:52,480
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

213
00:14:52,907 --> 00:14:54,608
Yay! Make a wish!

214
00:15:04,131 --> 00:15:05,760
I don't see my prayer has been answered.

215
00:15:06,478 --> 00:15:07,760
What did you wish for?

216
00:15:08,563 --> 00:15:11,080
I wished you'd leave Thailand

217
00:15:12,659 --> 00:15:14,680
and come live here with me. Right now.

218
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:16,661
Oh, come on. Don't be so dramatic.

219
00:15:16,851 --> 00:15:19,160
I'll come back as soon as I've taken care of everything.

220
00:15:19,806 --> 00:15:21,000
Is your sister's business

221
00:15:22,054 --> 00:15:24,240
so important that you have to abandon your work and me?

222
00:15:26,502 --> 00:15:29,830
Andrew, she's my only sister.

223
00:15:30,427 --> 00:15:31,840
And I'm not leaving you.

224
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,200
Yeah, I understand that just

225
00:15:36,774 --> 00:15:38,240
I need time to accept it, you know?

226
00:15:39,494 --> 00:15:40,800
I will waiting for you, Nina.

227
00:15:41,515 --> 00:15:42,816
I'm waiting for that, too.

228
00:15:46,263 --> 00:15:48,500
Nina, what's that ring?

229
00:15:51,987 --> 00:15:54,560
It's just a toy ring. I bought it for fun.

230
00:16:01,952 --> 00:16:03,320
You've got quite the connections, haven't you?

231
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:05,701
Huh?

232
00:16:06,014 --> 00:16:07,518
Last time, it was a hospital director.

233
00:16:07,886 --> 00:16:09,107
This time, it's a police inspector.

234
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,800
Who's next? The Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces?

235
00:16:12,552 --> 00:16:14,678
How could you bully her like that?

236
00:16:14,918 --> 00:16:16,976
Ta is just a defenseless young woman, Nopnapha!

237
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:24,484
What?

238
00:16:36,048 --> 00:16:38,678
Hey, Nopnapha! Have you lost your mind?

239
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:43,200
Hey! Don't you dare! Don't!

240
00:16:43,211 --> 00:16:44,212
Goddamn it!

241
00:16:46,595 --> 00:16:48,158
Hey, what's that noise?

242
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,760
You think you're the only one who can go crazy?

243
00:16:59,283 --> 00:17:00,560
I can go crazy, too, damn it!

244
00:17:03,363 --> 00:17:05,440
How do you like that? Huh?

245
00:17:06,768 --> 00:17:08,440
So now you're swearing at me, huh?

246
00:17:08,838 --> 00:17:09,839
Damn right!

247
00:17:12,139 --> 00:17:13,480
What are you gonna do about it?

248
00:17:16,294 --> 00:17:18,832
- Mom! Hurry and stop them!
- Let's go!

249
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:22,080
Having an identical copy of the ring you gave me
made for that bitch was insulting enough!

250
00:17:22,102 --> 00:17:23,640
And her diamond is even more expensive than mine!

251
00:17:24,886 --> 00:17:27,200
Oh, so that's what this is about. You're just being greedy!

252
00:17:27,286 --> 00:17:28,640
This isn't about the money, damn it!

253
00:17:28,918 --> 00:17:31,320
It's about you valuing that damn mistress

254
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:32,710
more than my dignity as your lawful wife!

255
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:35,621
Haven't you figured it out yet? I love Ta!

256
00:17:35,641 --> 00:17:37,642
Of course I want to give her the very best!

257
00:17:37,699 --> 00:17:39,800
As for all that nonsense about your dignity and pride,

258
00:17:39,843 --> 00:17:41,644
that's just something you've made up in your head!

259
00:17:41,704 --> 00:17:42,718
You're driving yourself crazy over nothing!

260
00:17:42,808 --> 00:17:45,040
Crazy, huh? You bastard, Jenphop! Take this!

261
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,000
Ouch! That hurts, damn it!

262
00:17:47,166 --> 00:17:49,120
Hey! I just had a hair transplant, damn it!

263
00:17:49,167 --> 00:17:50,368
Like I give a damn!

264
00:17:50,494 --> 00:17:52,960
Ouch! That fucking hurts, you know!

265
00:17:53,422 --> 00:17:54,440
My hair's all messed up!

266
00:17:54,974 --> 00:17:57,040
I love Ta! Didn't you hear me?

267
00:17:57,550 --> 00:17:58,920
You're supposed to love me!

268
00:17:59,659 --> 00:18:02,520
- Uncle! Uncle!
- Stop scratching me!

269
00:18:02,566 --> 00:18:04,680
That's enough! Both of you, stop!

270
00:18:05,963 --> 00:18:07,640
- Are you okay?
- Clean up this house right now!

271
00:18:08,574 --> 00:18:11,270
A TV crew is coming to film tomorrow. Have you forgotten?

272
00:18:11,275 --> 00:18:12,766
Oh, that's perfect.

273
00:18:12,931 --> 00:18:15,320
Tomorrow, I'll take them on a tour of our bedrooms.

274
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:17,071
I'll let the whole country know

275
00:18:17,525 --> 00:18:19,326
that this so-called model family

276
00:18:19,384 --> 00:18:21,120
has a husband and wife who sleep in separate rooms.

277
00:18:22,606 --> 00:18:24,160
You think you'd actually dare say that?

278
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,940
- You're all talk!
- Wanna bet?

279
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,520
Go ahead, pick whichever show you want!

280
00:18:27,568 --> 00:18:30,480
How about Rueang Yai Rai Wan? Or Jud? What about Jud?

281
00:18:30,582 --> 00:18:32,250
Jud, the one who digs out every truth!

282
00:18:32,283 --> 00:18:33,284
Phop.

283
00:18:34,491 --> 00:18:36,752
Family isn't something to joke about.

284
00:18:37,092 --> 00:18:39,087
Think about your children, too.

285
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,400
Don't let a moment of anger

286
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:43,518
destroy our family, Phop.

287
00:18:43,651 --> 00:18:45,280
Oh, come on. There's nothing left to destroy!

288
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,560
The kids already know exactly what their parents are like.

289
00:18:47,942 --> 00:18:50,440
Two rotten peas in a pod aren't going to split up that easily.

290
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:53,240
So we'll just have to keep living like this!

291
00:18:53,915 --> 00:18:57,360
Besides, if we divorced, who would get you promoted, huh?

292
00:18:57,728 --> 00:18:59,480
That's right! If we got divorced,

293
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:03,480
your three-time Perfect Woman of the Year award

294
00:19:03,542 --> 00:19:04,560
would be taken away!

295
00:19:05,366 --> 00:19:08,216
Your ego is bigger than Mount Everest!

296
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,130
And your skin is thinner than a sheet of paper!

297
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:12,080
No matter how much of a bastard I am,

298
00:19:12,238 --> 00:19:15,300
you'll never divorce me!

299
00:19:15,752 --> 00:19:17,840
Jenphop, get over here!

300
00:19:18,053 --> 00:19:20,395
- How dare you treat me like this?
- You've torn my shirt to shreds!

301
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,401
That hurts, damn it!

302
00:19:22,502 --> 00:19:24,803
- Mom! Dad!
- Tell her to stop!

303
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:26,864
Titus, stay back, sweetheart! There's broken glass here.

304
00:19:28,566 --> 00:19:30,300
What should I wear tomorrow?

305
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,200
Oh, just wear pink!

306
00:19:32,221 --> 00:19:35,259
What pink? I think white looks better!

307
00:19:35,702 --> 00:19:37,520
Dad, you choose!

308
00:19:44,955 --> 00:19:46,640
Pink, sweetheart. It's prettier.

309
00:19:47,414 --> 00:19:50,360
Can you help me pick my outfit too? I can also fix my hair.

310
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:53,600
Some bitch just messed up my hair.

311
00:19:54,478 --> 00:19:56,560
- Still calling me a dog?
- Come on, let's go.

312
00:19:57,454 --> 00:19:58,600
Jenphop, you bastard!

313
00:19:59,558 --> 00:20:00,559
Uncle, that's enough.

314
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:04,635
I was more shocked by Phop, actually.

315
00:20:04,998 --> 00:20:06,600
Who goes up and talks to Mickey Mouse?

316
00:20:06,672 --> 00:20:09,000
And he just kept talking to him nonstop.

317
00:20:09,544 --> 00:20:11,560
Well, I was completely freaking out.

318
00:20:12,072 --> 00:20:14,558
And the only staff member around was Mickey Mouse.

319
00:20:14,808 --> 00:20:15,889
So I went up to him and asked,

320
00:20:16,531 --> 00:20:18,040
Have you seen my daughter?

321
00:20:18,147 --> 00:20:20,680
She's about this tall, wearing these clothes.

322
00:20:20,768 --> 00:20:22,200
Right. And did he answer you?

323
00:20:22,344 --> 00:20:25,720
How could he? He's Mickey Mouse. All he could do was gesture.

324
00:20:25,910 --> 00:20:28,203
In the end, he took us to the information desk.

325
00:20:28,550 --> 00:20:31,000
Yes, Donald Duck brought me back to my parents.

326
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:34,680
Yes, I was the one who found her talking to Donald Duck.

327
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:37,606
The father was talking to Mickey Mouse,

328
00:20:37,779 --> 00:20:40,780
and the daughter to Donald Duck. What a family!

329
00:20:42,520 --> 00:20:46,800
Well, today we've truly experienced all the love and warmth that fills this home.

330
00:20:46,821 --> 00:20:48,320
We've certainly had our fill of it.

331
00:20:48,451 --> 00:20:49,640
And finally,

332
00:20:49,726 --> 00:20:52,560
with divorce rates continuing to rise in Thai society,

333
00:20:52,627 --> 00:20:55,640
could you share some advice for families facing difficulties?

334
00:20:55,934 --> 00:20:57,816
It's just like governing a country.

335
00:20:58,211 --> 00:20:59,560
You have to put the common good first.

336
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,041
Whatever we're thinking about,

337
00:21:01,590 --> 00:21:03,760
deciding on, or planning to do

338
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:07,400
should benefit everyone in the family, not just ourselves.

339
00:21:07,521 --> 00:21:09,440
That's how a family can stay together.

340
00:21:15,051 --> 00:21:19,080
Let me stop and buy some fruit. I'm craving something sour.

341
00:21:19,397 --> 00:21:21,339
Chuenchom, are you pregnant?

342
00:21:21,398 --> 00:21:22,800
Well, that's possible.

343
00:21:22,912 --> 00:21:25,520
Then I'll have a mango, please.

344
00:21:25,639 --> 00:21:28,240
Make it so sour it'll turn my pee into acid.

345
00:21:28,726 --> 00:21:30,902
As for me, I'd like some

346
00:21:31,094 --> 00:21:33,366
Sato Nishiki cherries, please.

347
00:21:33,531 --> 00:21:36,960
Why don't you open your eyes and see if she even sells cherries?

348
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:39,400
And with a face like yours, Cha-am,

349
00:21:39,504 --> 00:21:42,880
you'd be better suited to wild berries or wood apples.

350
00:21:44,414 --> 00:21:45,566
Chuenchom,

351
00:21:45,902 --> 00:21:50,051
stop projecting your own nasty nature onto others.

352
00:21:51,903 --> 00:21:53,804
Ma'am, I've changed my mind.

353
00:21:53,904 --> 00:21:56,664
I'll have one Indian olive and

354
00:21:56,771 --> 00:21:59,400
one coconut, please. Because drinking coconut water

355
00:21:59,539 --> 00:22:01,360
makes your skin look beautiful.

356
00:22:01,752 --> 00:22:03,086
Oh, by the way,

357
00:22:03,368 --> 00:22:07,672
did you watch the show yesterday featuring the Minister, the Director, and their children?

358
00:22:08,056 --> 00:22:09,064
Aren't they lovely?

359
00:22:10,248 --> 00:22:11,760
She's so good at her job.

360
00:22:12,211 --> 00:22:15,080
And they're a model family for the whole country!

361
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:18,601
Yes.

362
00:22:18,627 --> 00:22:21,520
But which part of their family should you follow as an example?

363
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:26,400
Haven't you heard all the gossip spreading like wildfire throughout the ministry?

364
00:22:26,528 --> 00:22:27,835
Oh, I don't believe any of that!

365
00:22:28,592 --> 00:22:31,200
If I ever hear anyone badmouthing the Minister's family,

366
00:22:31,250 --> 00:22:33,051
I'll slash their mouth with a knife!

367
00:22:35,787 --> 00:22:36,788
Here.

368
00:22:36,939 --> 00:22:40,280
Take some fruit to the Minister and the Director for me.

369
00:22:41,099 --> 00:22:43,600
- You see them at work, right?
- Yes.

370
00:22:43,702 --> 00:22:45,120
We see them every day.

371
00:22:45,150 --> 00:22:46,711
I'll make sure to tell them

372
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,680
that Aunt Lamai from the fruit stall sent these.

373
00:22:49,824 --> 00:22:51,440
I'm sure they'll be delighted.

374
00:22:52,096 --> 00:22:54,176
Oh, does that mean

375
00:22:54,272 --> 00:22:58,520
our kind Aunt Lamai is giving us all this for free?

376
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,120
That's 80 baht, dear.

377
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,360
- 80?
- Yep.

378
00:23:04,970 --> 00:23:06,200
Pay for me first, okay?

379
00:23:07,371 --> 00:23:10,072
Hey, old lady! Did you watch the Director's interview?

380
00:23:10,208 --> 00:23:12,320
- It's got millions of views!
- I saw it.

381
00:23:13,168 --> 00:23:15,960
Of course, ordinary people who don't know what we know

382
00:23:16,009 --> 00:23:17,238
are showering them with praise.

383
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:21,361
But those of us who know the truth can't say a thing, can we?

384
00:23:21,472 --> 00:23:23,300
I've got a million things I wish I could say.

385
00:23:23,330 --> 00:23:24,331
So true, Auntie.

386
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:29,654
Everyone, I brought you some fruit!

387
00:23:31,579 --> 00:23:33,228
Isn't anyone going to thank me?

388
00:23:34,232 --> 00:23:36,120
Cha-am, could you stop lying?

389
00:23:36,328 --> 00:23:39,329
Everyone, I paid for half of it.

390
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:42,560
Both of you, stop lying!

391
00:23:42,581 --> 00:23:45,440
How could lowly employees like you afford to buy anything?

392
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:47,000
The vendor gave it to you for free, didn't she?

393
00:23:48,096 --> 00:23:52,288
And how would a high-and-mighty employee like you know that?

394
00:23:52,739 --> 00:23:55,747
Oh, just look at all the snacks on this table.

395
00:23:55,750 --> 00:23:58,643
The vendors sent them all for the Director and the Minister.

396
00:23:58,718 --> 00:24:03,380
They said they watched the show last night and became huge fans.

397
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:09,960
I wonder when I'll ever be as beautiful and successful as the Minister.

398
00:24:10,246 --> 00:24:13,160
And on top of that, she has such a handsome, sexy husband.

399
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:16,500
Talk about being truly blessed, right?

400
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:17,311
You're right.

401
00:24:17,366 --> 00:24:22,118
Oh, but would you still want him if he had a mistress?

402
00:24:22,247 --> 00:24:23,440
Would you?

403
00:24:26,611 --> 00:24:28,040
Wow, Auntie! That's harsh.

404
00:24:28,387 --> 00:24:30,040
But everyone,

405
00:24:30,456 --> 00:24:32,664
the mistress doesn't seem to have affected the Minister at all.

406
00:24:32,863 --> 00:24:36,164
Ever since Ta came back, they still seem very much in love.

407
00:24:36,291 --> 00:24:38,264
They're even being all lovey-dovey on TV.

408
00:24:42,174 --> 00:24:44,963
Don't rub salt in Ta's wounds like that, Chom.

409
00:24:45,955 --> 00:24:49,155
Have some sympathy for her. Poor thing.

410
00:24:50,856 --> 00:24:52,857
I'm sorry, Ta. It's just that last night,

411
00:24:53,038 --> 00:24:56,239
I took a little too much estrogen, so I'm a bit out of it.

412
00:25:06,283 --> 00:25:07,284
Director.

413
00:25:08,822 --> 00:25:10,300
Let's have dinner together tonight.

414
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:16,497
I heard it loud and clear with my own two ears, ma'am.

415
00:25:16,912 --> 00:25:18,760
How shameless can she be?

416
00:25:18,827 --> 00:25:22,038
Inviting another woman's husband to a hotel for sex.

417
00:25:22,315 --> 00:25:24,203
If I were his wife,

418
00:25:24,507 --> 00:25:27,120
I'd be absolutely devastated!

419
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:32,971
- Touch.
- Yes?

420
00:25:33,530 --> 00:25:36,035
Go to the meeting with Mr. Chen tonight in my place.

421
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:38,401
Make sure he understands

422
00:25:39,566 --> 00:25:42,979
that he can cut corners on materials, but the building must not collapse.

423
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,080
I'm going to deal with that bitch Mutta.

424
00:25:46,435 --> 00:25:49,200
Ma'am, I think something's suspicious.

425
00:25:50,515 --> 00:25:52,916
Normally, when Mutta arranges to meet the Director,

426
00:25:53,224 --> 00:25:55,320
she never talks on the phone where others can easily overhear her.

427
00:25:55,926 --> 00:25:59,200
But this time, it was as if she deliberately let someone overhear

428
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:01,240
and report it to you.

429
00:26:02,427 --> 00:26:03,798
Be careful. You might be walking into her trap.

430
00:26:05,192 --> 00:26:06,193
I don't care.

431
00:26:07,422 --> 00:26:10,800
I want to see what kind of trap she's set for me.

432
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:17,801
Ta.

433
00:26:20,838 --> 00:26:24,534
My sweet Ta, don't be mad at me anymore.

434
00:26:25,534 --> 00:26:26,963
Nopnapha was trying to sabotage me.

435
00:26:27,582 --> 00:26:29,784
She kept me from going to the police station to help you.

436
00:26:31,491 --> 00:26:32,787
That's not what I'm upset about.

437
00:26:35,392 --> 00:26:37,942
Then what are you upset about? So I can make it up to you.

438
00:26:40,742 --> 00:26:44,043
You once told me that if Nopnapha ever hurt me again,

439
00:26:45,078 --> 00:26:47,165
you'd publicly announce your separation from her.

440
00:26:50,352 --> 00:26:51,856
I watched your interview yesterday.

441
00:26:52,838 --> 00:26:54,480
Everyone on that show was laughing.

442
00:26:55,568 --> 00:26:56,569
I was the only one

443
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:58,720
left crying all alone.

444
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:03,000
Were you deliberately giving me false hope, Director?

445
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:04,041
Ta.

446
00:27:04,630 --> 00:27:05,831
I'm a man of my word.

447
00:27:06,323 --> 00:27:07,680
I always keep my promises.

448
00:27:08,638 --> 00:27:10,680
But I'm also the father of those two children.

449
00:27:11,667 --> 00:27:14,424
How would they feel if I announced on TV that I'd left their mother?

450
00:27:14,810 --> 00:27:16,880
How do you think those two kids would feel, Ta?

451
00:27:18,611 --> 00:27:21,240
You can't protect your children's feelings forever, Director.

452
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:24,590
They have to know their parents are going to separate.

453
00:27:25,059 --> 00:27:26,400
And however they feel about it,

454
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:28,819
they'll have to learn to deal with those feelings themselves.

455
00:27:33,475 --> 00:27:35,176
I've never seen this side of you before.

456
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:39,760
You've never pressured me this much to leave Nopnapha before.

457
00:27:41,456 --> 00:27:45,120
Didn't you say you'd wait for me no matter how long it took?

458
00:27:47,408 --> 00:27:50,129
Ta, I found a plot of land in Khao Yai.

459
00:27:50,486 --> 00:27:53,240
The view is gorgeous, and the price is great. Andrew likes it, too.

460
00:27:53,494 --> 00:27:54,560
I'll send you the details.

461
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:57,600
Sure, send them over.

462
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:00,328
Show your boyfriend, too, and see if he likes it.

463
00:28:00,563 --> 00:28:03,934
Or the four of us could have a video call and share our thoughts.

464
00:28:07,827 --> 00:28:08,828
Well...

465
00:28:11,224 --> 00:28:12,830
I'm not so sure about my boyfriend anymore.

466
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:16,000
Not sure? What do you mean?

467
00:28:24,592 --> 00:28:27,960
Ta, what's wrong? Why are you crying?

468
00:28:33,547 --> 00:28:35,440
How long have you been telling me to wait, Director?

469
00:28:36,779 --> 00:28:40,032
Do you have any idea what it feels like to wait without knowing when it'll end?

470
00:28:41,942 --> 00:28:44,160
What's gotten into you, Ta? Why are you so angry with me?

471
00:28:47,051 --> 00:28:49,464
And why don't you think about everything I've done for you?

472
00:28:50,259 --> 00:28:52,236
How much have I spent on all those designer things I bought you?

473
00:28:52,536 --> 00:28:54,088
Not to mention all the money I've given you.

474
00:28:54,419 --> 00:28:56,572
You said you'd save it to buy a house for us.

475
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,168
Huh, Ta?

476
00:28:58,867 --> 00:29:00,880
If I weren't serious about us, would I have invested so much?

477
00:29:00,990 --> 00:29:02,190
So you just threw money at me, right?

478
00:29:02,766 --> 00:29:04,088
To keep me tied to you

479
00:29:04,510 --> 00:29:05,944
and keep giving me false hope,

480
00:29:06,371 --> 00:29:09,491
when you never actually intended to leave your wife, did you?

481
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:16,125
Why are you talking to me like this?

482
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:20,601
Do you realize how much you've changed?

483
00:29:25,486 --> 00:29:29,259
You're nothing like the Ta I used to know. What's gotten into you?

484
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:39,787
I just...

485
00:29:42,512 --> 00:29:45,680
I just want our relationship to move forward.

486
00:29:50,635 --> 00:29:53,131
I don't want to keep hiding our love.

487
00:29:56,992 --> 00:29:57,993
I...

488
00:29:59,739 --> 00:30:01,480
I want a future with you, Director.

489
00:30:33,382 --> 00:30:34,383
Let's have a drink.

490
00:30:59,118 --> 00:31:00,119
My sweet Ta.

491
00:31:00,264 --> 00:31:01,265
Director.

492
00:31:08,818 --> 00:31:10,820
- Slow down, Director.
- Ta.

493
00:31:10,862 --> 00:31:12,880
- I've missed you so much.
- Director.

494
00:31:15,070 --> 00:31:16,871
- I can't hold back anymore.
- Director.

495
00:31:17,471 --> 00:31:18,880
You smell so good, Ta.

496
00:31:27,167 --> 00:31:28,720
I'm going to give it to you good tonight.

497
00:31:29,184 --> 00:31:30,185
Ta.

498
00:31:30,928 --> 00:31:32,360
Slow down, Director.

499
00:31:35,670 --> 00:31:36,920
Follow me.

500
00:31:48,296 --> 00:31:51,320
Director, let me undress you.

501
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:54,601
Okay, okay.

502
00:32:05,411 --> 00:32:07,720
I can't hold back much longer.

503
00:32:15,739 --> 00:32:18,820
Easy, Director. You've already left bruises all over me.

504
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:23,019
Director, I've got a little surprise for you.

505
00:32:23,739 --> 00:32:25,160
To make things more exciting.

506
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:27,560
Just give me a moment.

507
00:32:28,715 --> 00:32:29,716
Director.

508
00:32:32,251 --> 00:32:34,680
You've got a surprise for me, Ta?

509
00:32:38,182 --> 00:32:40,520
You know what Director stands for? Damn Irresistible Husband!

510
00:33:00,427 --> 00:33:03,048
Catch this, Director.

511
00:33:07,392 --> 00:33:08,393
Ta.

512
00:33:11,430 --> 00:33:13,480
- My sweet Ta!
- Here's the last piece.

513
00:33:16,859 --> 00:33:18,760
Wow, Ta!

514
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,041
My sweet Ta.

515
00:33:22,403 --> 00:33:24,296
I can't take much more of this, Ta!

516
00:33:25,459 --> 00:33:27,651
If you want to have fun, you'll have to be patient, Director.

517
00:33:29,707 --> 00:33:32,040
Ta, I'm almost there.

518
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,800
If you don't hurry up,

519
